Finally. I've been playing for about 2 years.

Some things regarding this game:

-Spellbook of identify helps a lot. I've been attacked by a mind flayer
and I don't know WTF would I've done without it. Any item is ready to
use/discard/stash almost instantly. 
-Vlad is lame.
-Got 4 amulets of life saving and never used them. I mean, I haven't
been killed once. Other games I would have paid anything for one.
-Real luck reaching my coaligned altar at Astral Plane on first try, and
guess, it was Famine's. Also, coaligned minetown altar.
-I hate disenchanters. I have been AC:-41, ascended AC:-37 because of
them.
-Someone should have told me that both money and gems are about useless
once you get to Gehennom, or at least, once you get the ascension kit.
-Croesus paid a hell of my divine protection, even when I was
Xp:15 or so.
-Lucky for a pair of bone piles, specially a monk's for his Eyes of the
Overworld (Gehennom is much simpler with it).
-Had to discard Mjollnir and Vorpal Blade because of weight.
-7 wishes from a single wand and 1 from a magic lamp.
-Had to face Orcus nasties on the escape with the amulet, since he
escaped upstairs when I was going down, and I took him for dead.
-Spellbook of finger of dead made Rodney a minor problem. Also, I got 2
wands of death.
-At the end game I found the Wizard more powerful with Grayswandir than
with attack spells (magic missile, cone of cold, fireball).
-BTW, not a single spellbook of drain life in the entire game. Weird.

